      "content": "ok but when u say \"no credible evidence\" that feels like a way to just shut down the conversation. if people are seeing things that look off or hearing about specific vulnerabilities in the chain of custody, isn't it fair to question it? it feels like the official \"consensus\" is just used to dismiss anyone who has legitimate concerns about how the votes are handled.",
