    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but if the system isn't 100% verifiable by everyone, then isn't the \"consensus\" just a way to keep people from looking too close? it seems like everytime someone points out a real flaw, the response is just \"the results were fine anyway,\" which doesn't actually address the security risk. if you had to pick, do you think the current system is actually robust enough to handle much more scrutiny, or is it fundamentally flawed? be real with me.",
